{"hits":{"hits":[{"id":"1918113","metadata":{"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Yau Mathematical Sciences Center, Tsinghua University, Beijing, China"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"kikuchi, ken","full_name":"Kikuchi, Ken","curated_relation":true,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/2062225"},"affiliations":[{"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/institutions/904826"},"value":"Tsinghua U., Beijing"}],"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"K.Kikuchi.3"}],"last_name":"Kikuchi","signature_block":"CACACk","first_name":"Ken","uuid":"bd691be5-0da7-459e-ac96-d23627fae8e0","recid":2062225}],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"We propose when and why symmetry enhancements happen in massless renormalization group (RG) flows to two-dimensional rational conformal field theories (RCFTs). We test our proposal against known RG flows from unitary minimal models. We also suggest which sign of the relevant coupling triggers the massless RG flow. The other sign triggers massive RG flows to topological quantum field theories (TQFTs). We comment on their ground state degeneracies.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"control_number":1918113,"preprint_date":"2021-09-06","titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Symmetry enhancement in RCFT"}],"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th","cond-mat.stat-mech","math.CT"],"value":"2109.02672"}],"document_type":["article"]},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1918113?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1918113?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1918113?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1918113?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1918113?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1918113?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1918113"},"updated":"2023-12-04T13:45:47.968495+00:00","created":"2021-0